<h1 class="text-4xl pb-4 border-b border-dashed border-terminal-dim">
  Classic Game Engine<span class="inline-block w-[12px] h-[26px] bg-terminal-green ml-[4px] mb-[-2px] animate-cursor-blink"></span>
</h1>

<p class="text-2xl pt-6 pb-4 text-terminal-bright">
  The Classic Game Engine powers text-based adventure games in Super Text Adventure. You define your entire game world as a JSON document, and the engine handles parsing player commands, managing state, and running all game mechanics.
</p>

<h2 class="text-3xl pt-6 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">What You Can Build</h2>

<div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-4">
  <div class="border border-terminal-dim rounded p-4">
    <div class="text-2xl text-terminal-bright pb-2">Explorable Worlds</div>
    <div class="text-xl text-terminal-dim">Rooms connected by exits with descriptions, hidden passages, locked doors, and directional navigation.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="border border-terminal-dim rounded p-4">
    <div class="text-2xl text-terminal-bright pb-2">Items & Inventory</div>
    <div class="text-xl text-terminal-dim">Pickupable items, containers with locks, weapons, healing potions, and items that interact with the world.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="border border-terminal-dim rounded p-4">
    <div class="text-2xl text-terminal-bright pb-2">NPCs & Quests</div>
    <div class="text-xl text-terminal-dim">Characters with branching dialogue trees, item trading, quest flags, gated conversations, and patrol movement.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="border border-terminal-dim rounded p-4">
    <div class="text-2xl text-terminal-bright pb-2">Combat & Dice</div>
    <div class="text-xl text-terminal-dim">Turn-based combat with initiative, attack/defend/flee, weapons, armor, D&D-style dice rolls, and hostile creatures that ambush the player.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">How It Works</h2>

<div class="pt-4 text-xl space-y-3">
  <p><span class="text-terminal-bright">1.</span> You write a JSON file describing your world &mdash; rooms, items, NPCs, and creatures.</p>
  <p><span class="text-terminal-bright">2.</span> The engine loads your JSON as the <code class="text-terminal-bright">world_data</code>.</p>
  <p><span class="text-terminal-bright">3.</span> Players type natural-language commands like <code class="text-terminal-bright">go north</code>, <code class="text-terminal-bright">take sword</code>, or <code class="text-terminal-bright">talk to wizard</code>.</p>
  <p><span class="text-terminal-bright">4.</span> The <strong>CommandParser</strong> translates input into structured commands (verb + target + modifier).</p>
  <p><span class="text-terminal-bright">5.</span> The <strong>Engine</strong> routes commands to the appropriate <strong>Handler</strong> (movement, items, combat, etc.).</p>
  <p><span class="text-terminal-bright">6.</span> The handler processes the command, updates game state, and returns a text response.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">Top-Level JSON Structure</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">Every game world is defined by a single JSON object with these top-level keys:</p>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green"><span class="comment">// world_data.json</span>
{
  <span class="key">"meta"</span>: {
    <span class="key">"name"</span>: <span class="str">"My Adventure"</span>,
    <span class="key">"description"</span>: <span class="str">"A short quest to retrieve the Crystal of Power."</span>,
    <span class="key">"starting_room"</span>: <span class="str">"tavern"</span>,
    <span class="key">"version"</span>: <span class="str">"1.0"</span>
  },
  <span class="key">"rooms"</span>:     { <span class="comment">/* room definitions */</span> },
  <span class="key">"items"</span>:     { <span class="comment">/* item definitions */</span> },
  <span class="key">"npcs"</span>:      { <span class="comment">/* NPC definitions */</span> },
  <span class="key">"creatures"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* creature definitions */</span> }
}</pre>

